1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,476
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,479 --> 00:00:02,917
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,294 --> 00:00:04,925
(Episode 20)

4
00:00:07,738 --> 00:00:09,305
- Planning meeting?
- Yeah.

5
00:00:09,665 --> 00:00:11,073
It's going to be two nights.

6
00:00:11,452 --> 00:00:14,765
We're relaunching our folktale series,
so the concept meetings are running long.

7
00:00:14,767 --> 00:00:17,162
Isn't the meeting just an excuse
for a vacation?

8
00:00:17,164 --> 00:00:19,672
No. We just started the company.

9
00:00:19,885 --> 00:00:21,681
The CEO isn't like that.

10
00:00:21,962 --> 00:00:24,504
He was in the Navy. A general, no less.

11
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,545
Really?

12
00:00:25,885 --> 00:00:27,389
Then why go into publishing?

13
00:00:27,392 --> 00:00:29,651
Are you sure it's legit?
You should look into it.

14
00:00:29,653 --> 00:00:32,751
- I just don't see the connection.
- And yours makes sense?

15
00:00:32,753 --> 00:00:35,118
You went from playing the cello
to running an entertainment company.

16
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:38,381
The same could be said about you.
Why are you only judging others?

17
00:00:38,745 --> 00:00:41,334
I actually trust
what the general says more.

18
00:00:41,739 --> 00:00:44,534
You little brat.
Why are you always picking on me?

19
00:00:45,005 --> 00:00:46,905
You started it.

20
00:00:47,792 --> 00:00:51,116
Anyway, I'm leaving tomorrow
and won't be back until after the weekend,

21
00:00:51,211 --> 00:00:53,358
so don't call or worry about me.

22
00:00:53,738 --> 00:00:57,625
I'll text you whenever
I get a chance, okay?

23
00:00:57,652 --> 00:00:59,365
Yes, got it.

24
00:01:00,445 --> 00:01:02,385
Having a job does have its perks.

25
00:01:02,387 --> 00:01:03,478
You don't nag me anymore.

26
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,481
Wait till you get your first paycheck.
I'm going to spend it all.

27
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:07,811
It's my paycheck.

28
00:01:08,605 --> 00:01:10,385
First paychecks belong to your parents.

29
00:01:10,411 --> 00:01:11,808
Who made that rule?

30
00:01:11,942 --> 00:01:13,597
It's in the Constitution.

31
00:01:13,741 --> 00:01:15,138
Look it up if you're curious.

32
00:01:25,305 --> 00:01:27,794
- What did you say?
- I told her I'd be going with Jung A,

33
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:29,461
so please cover for me.

34
00:01:30,483 --> 00:01:32,494
- I'm asking you for a favor.
- Are you really going to do it?

35
00:01:34,912 --> 00:01:37,859
I saw him being taken
to the emergency room yesterday.

36
00:01:38,072 --> 00:01:41,912
I can't turn a blind eye anymore.

37
00:01:42,698 --> 00:01:44,869
Even if my mom beats me to death,

38
00:01:44,945 --> 00:01:46,385
I want to save O Reum.

39
00:01:47,558 --> 00:01:49,215
Don't you understand how I feel?

40
00:01:49,218 --> 00:01:52,345
- Am I really being a bad child?
- Hey, hold on.

41
00:01:53,098 --> 00:01:55,497
How am I supposed to answer
all those questions at once?

42
00:01:58,030 --> 00:01:59,445
Anyway, that's amazing.

43
00:01:59,558 --> 00:02:01,211
I don't think I could ever do that.

44
00:02:01,218 --> 00:02:03,587
If I had something
that could save someone,

45
00:02:04,932 --> 00:02:07,625
I couldn't just let them die.

46
00:02:09,398 --> 00:02:10,918
Since it's the weekend,

47
00:02:11,051 --> 00:02:12,918
I'll talk to the CEO.

48
00:02:13,862 --> 00:02:14,878
Thank you.

49
00:02:16,238 --> 00:02:17,263
But...

50
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:20,898
are there any side effects?
Are you sure you're okay?

51
00:02:21,125 --> 00:02:22,531
As far as I know, there aren't any.

52
00:02:22,885 --> 00:02:24,165
Don't worry.

53
00:02:25,398 --> 00:02:27,943
I'll introduce you to O Reum someday.

54
00:02:27,945 --> 00:02:29,410
He's really adorable.

55
00:02:31,592 --> 00:02:33,208
I also got a lot of ideas for our book...

56
00:02:33,210 --> 00:02:35,382
while spending time with him.

57
00:02:36,474 --> 00:02:37,490
Then,

58
00:02:38,211 --> 00:02:39,331
I'll leave it to you.

59
00:02:43,998 --> 00:02:48,118
She's Mother Teresa. Audrey Hepburn.

60
00:02:49,045 --> 00:02:52,051
Na Ji Ni, I really admire you.

61
00:03:00,558 --> 00:03:01,571
Have a seat.

62
00:03:01,679 --> 00:03:03,579
This is O Reum's doctor.

63
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:05,631
- Hello.
- Hello.

64
00:03:05,985 --> 00:03:07,805
You've made your decision, right?

65
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:10,702
- Yes.
- You're like an aunt to him...

66
00:03:11,025 --> 00:03:13,218
- Something like that.
- It's complicated.

67
00:03:14,605 --> 00:03:16,741
The process is simple for family,

68
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:18,239
but complicated for outsiders.

69
00:03:21,038 --> 00:03:23,883
When will O Reum's family find out?

70
00:03:23,885 --> 00:03:25,807
Considering the donor's health,

71
00:03:25,809 --> 00:03:28,611
we'll collect the cells first
to make sure it's safe.

72
00:03:28,772 --> 00:03:30,671
Then we'll proceed with the transplant.

73
00:03:33,598 --> 00:03:35,212
Please take care of it.

74
00:03:36,465 --> 00:03:38,175
- I'm counting on you.
- Okay.

75
00:03:38,178 --> 00:03:40,818
- I'll visit the hospital room later.
- Okay.

76
00:03:54,338 --> 00:03:56,466
I heard there was a guest.
I wondered who it was.

77
00:03:57,385 --> 00:03:59,487
If it's about the bone marrow,
don't even bring it up.

78
00:03:59,490 --> 00:04:01,711
If you're here to work,
I'll think about it.

79
00:04:01,906 --> 00:04:04,576
No matter how much I deny it,
you two are still his sons.

80
00:04:04,578 --> 00:04:05,581
And...

81
00:04:06,802 --> 00:04:08,331
because I'm not experienced enough.

82
00:04:08,903 --> 00:04:10,571
We're here about the bone marrow.

83
00:04:10,678 --> 00:04:12,671
- Then there's nothing to discuss.
- Please.

84
00:04:13,385 --> 00:04:15,944
- Please let her at least get tested.
- If she gets tested,

85
00:04:16,075 --> 00:04:19,105
and she's a match,
you'll come by more often, right?

86
00:04:19,398 --> 00:04:22,758
That awful Vietnamese daughter-in-law
is going to come here and cause a scene.

87
00:04:23,532 --> 00:04:25,161
She came to take the apartment before,

88
00:04:25,163 --> 00:04:26,851
and now she's coming
to take my daughter's bone marrow?

89
00:04:26,853 --> 00:04:28,285
That might not be the case.

90
00:04:29,065 --> 00:04:31,065
Then maybe both sides could let this go.

91
00:04:31,612 --> 00:04:33,704
That's why I'm asking you.

92
00:04:33,852 --> 00:04:35,019
Even in the worst-case scenario,

93
00:04:35,467 --> 00:04:37,926
if we can't find a donor and lose O Reum,

94
00:04:38,285 --> 00:04:39,945
I don't want to live with regret.

95
00:04:40,572 --> 00:04:42,608
I don't want to wonder...

96
00:04:43,209 --> 00:04:44,698
if we ignored our last bit of hope.

97
00:04:45,358 --> 00:04:47,874
- That's your family's problem.
- Please, I'm begging you.

98
00:04:48,332 --> 00:04:49,960
At least let us check.

99
00:04:52,212 --> 00:04:53,762
Tell Yeong Ju to come.

100
00:04:53,765 --> 00:04:55,898
Tell her to get on her knees and beg.

101
00:04:56,178 --> 00:04:59,298
She already came once, didn't she?

102
00:04:59,445 --> 00:05:01,242
I'm not asking her to beg.

103
00:05:01,487 --> 00:05:03,794
I want her to apologize...

104
00:05:03,929 --> 00:05:06,803
for cursing me when I gave birth to Ji Ni,

105
00:05:06,997 --> 00:05:08,954
for verbally abusing me
when I hadn't even recovered yet.

106
00:05:09,432 --> 00:05:12,281
- Well, back then...
- I still dream about it.

107
00:05:12,945 --> 00:05:16,067
I see myself kneeling in front of her.

108
00:05:16,352 --> 00:05:18,899
Begging her to at least accept Ji Ni
as part of the Cha family.

109
00:05:19,794 --> 00:05:21,014
I'm sorry.

110
00:05:22,052 --> 00:05:24,805
Please, just this once, be understanding.

111
00:05:24,845 --> 00:05:27,017
What did you say to Ji Ni?

112
00:05:27,051 --> 00:05:28,702
I can't even bring myself to repeat it.

113
00:05:28,952 --> 00:05:31,544
How could you say something like that
to a middle school girl?

114
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:34,125
It's horrifying.

115
00:05:34,753 --> 00:05:36,695
No. Absolutely not.

116
00:05:36,992 --> 00:05:40,961
Whether Ji Ni is a match or not,
it's still a no.

117
00:05:42,245 --> 00:05:45,336
- I don't want to know or check.
- Please, just for O Reum...

118
00:05:53,381 --> 00:05:55,128
I'm sorry for everything.

119
00:05:55,245 --> 00:05:57,013
For calling Ji Ni a jerk,

120
00:05:57,630 --> 00:05:59,090
for dumping trash on her,

121
00:05:59,692 --> 00:06:00,870
I apologize for all of it.

122
00:06:02,106 --> 00:06:03,211
I was wrong.

123
00:06:04,492 --> 00:06:05,511
Yeah,

124
00:06:05,985 --> 00:06:08,688
I felt sorry for O Reum too.

125
00:06:09,889 --> 00:06:10,898
You did?

126
00:06:10,978 --> 00:06:14,323
I once begged everyone
to put Ji Ni before me.

127
00:06:14,325 --> 00:06:15,858
How could I forget that?

128
00:06:15,992 --> 00:06:17,811
And he was...

129
00:06:18,045 --> 00:06:20,640
the first and only grandson
my husband ever got to hold.

130
00:06:20,817 --> 00:06:22,161
What did that child ever do
to deserve this?

131
00:06:23,345 --> 00:06:26,251
But we can't get entangled like this.

132
00:06:28,852 --> 00:06:31,018
Do you think an apology erases the past?

133
00:06:31,932 --> 00:06:32,951
No.

134
00:06:33,886 --> 00:06:34,931
Let's stop here.

135
00:06:45,465 --> 00:06:48,474
I'll come back tomorrow, Seung Hyun.
And the day after that.

136
00:06:48,758 --> 00:06:50,012
I'll keep begging if I have to.

137
00:06:51,191 --> 00:06:53,071
If mom comes and apologizes,

138
00:06:54,173 --> 00:06:56,056
she said she'd reconsider, right?

139
00:06:56,199 --> 00:06:58,398
Seung Hyun, get a grip.

140
00:06:58,498 --> 00:07:00,312
She just said that without thinking.

141
00:07:00,645 --> 00:07:02,170
Even if she did,

142
00:07:03,371 --> 00:07:05,021
maybe if we hold on to it,
she'll keep her word?

143
00:07:05,718 --> 00:07:07,032
I'll do it.

144
00:07:07,525 --> 00:07:09,631
I'll beg until my palms wear out,

145
00:07:10,528 --> 00:07:12,258
so let's not drag mom into this again.

146
00:07:13,132 --> 00:07:14,698
She already went once.

147
00:07:15,398 --> 00:07:16,806
She already went to their house.

148
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:19,421
Stop.

149
00:07:21,209 --> 00:07:22,211
Yeah...

150
00:07:23,399 --> 00:07:24,591
We should stop.

151
00:07:28,972 --> 00:07:31,951
They say, "Even if the sky falls,
there's still a way out."

152
00:07:32,172 --> 00:07:33,445
Don't lose hope.

153
00:07:42,072 --> 00:07:44,957
Let's get some cold noodles
or something refreshing.

154
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:48,327
And shave, will you?

155
00:07:59,978 --> 00:08:01,071
Enjoy your meal.

156
00:08:06,658 --> 00:08:08,154
Eat something.

157
00:08:08,255 --> 00:08:09,798
You're going to collapse first.

158
00:08:22,252 --> 00:08:23,274
O Reum...

159
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:25,832
used to love cold noodles.

160
00:08:25,834 --> 00:08:27,873
Just eat without thinking.

161
00:08:28,215 --> 00:08:30,083
You need strength
to go back and take care of him.

162
00:08:31,594 --> 00:08:32,618
Thanks.

163
00:08:32,831 --> 00:08:33,846
For begging...

164
00:08:34,196 --> 00:08:35,493
in my place earlier.

165
00:08:36,892 --> 00:08:39,198
You got on your knees
in front of that man too.

166
00:08:39,238 --> 00:08:40,788
If I could've,

167
00:08:41,362 --> 00:08:42,703
I would've done the same.

168
00:08:42,705 --> 00:08:44,458
She said it wouldn't matter if we went.

169
00:08:46,445 --> 00:08:48,734
So what, we're supposed
to send mom to beg again?

170
00:09:16,958 --> 00:09:19,594
First the off-key singing practice,
and now the cello?

171
00:09:21,625 --> 00:09:24,139
It's out of the frying pan
and into the fire.

172
00:09:38,305 --> 00:09:39,941
Sir, your meal is ready.

173
00:09:40,415 --> 00:09:41,825
Okay. Thank you.

174
00:09:41,827 --> 00:09:42,852
What about you, Su Jeong?

175
00:09:43,392 --> 00:09:44,598
I ordered mine too.

176
00:09:45,178 --> 00:09:48,959
- So you're finally taking up the cello?
- Yes. I've wanted to try it,

177
00:09:48,972 --> 00:09:52,045
and someone was selling one,
so I grabbed it. It's really hard.

178
00:09:52,047 --> 00:09:53,853
I think you're holding the bow wrong.

179
00:09:54,021 --> 00:09:55,212
Did you learn the cello?

180
00:09:55,712 --> 00:09:57,139
My sister knows how to play it.

181
00:09:57,531 --> 00:10:00,211
I got so sick
of hearing her practice at home...

182
00:10:00,485 --> 00:10:01,798
What did you learn, Su Jeong?

183
00:10:02,438 --> 00:10:03,725
I don't like music.

184
00:10:03,727 --> 00:10:06,105
You must not get along with your sister.

185
00:10:06,107 --> 00:10:09,165
- Then that woman who comes here...
- Mrs. Na Se Ri?

186
00:10:09,292 --> 00:10:10,887
My sister really likes her.

187
00:10:11,458 --> 00:10:12,645
Please don't mention it.

188
00:10:13,278 --> 00:10:15,954
If you like music that much,
you should've gone to music school.

189
00:10:15,957 --> 00:10:17,724
I wanted to. But...

190
00:10:18,145 --> 00:10:20,205
my grades were too good,
so I ended up studying something else.

191
00:10:23,172 --> 00:10:24,298
My lunch delivery is here.

192
00:10:25,072 --> 00:10:27,098
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

193
00:10:33,885 --> 00:10:36,705
Softly, like you're cradling it.

194
00:10:57,025 --> 00:10:58,213
Are you back?

195
00:10:59,507 --> 00:11:00,534
Yes.

196
00:11:01,595 --> 00:11:03,403
I went with Seung Woo.

197
00:11:04,984 --> 00:11:06,138
It was no use, right?

198
00:11:07,318 --> 00:11:09,105
She only brought up the past.

199
00:11:09,632 --> 00:11:10,698
What past?

200
00:11:10,845 --> 00:11:12,611
That she begged you too...

201
00:11:14,165 --> 00:11:15,205
That wicked girl.

202
00:11:15,645 --> 00:11:17,985
If she's saying no, just say no.
Why bring up the past?

203
00:11:23,358 --> 00:11:24,368
What?

204
00:11:24,495 --> 00:11:25,627
She said if you come,

205
00:11:27,095 --> 00:11:29,185
and apologize for what you said
when Ji Ni was born,

206
00:11:29,595 --> 00:11:31,293
- she'll think about it.
- What?

207
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:34,811
- Does that make sense?
- Exactly.

208
00:11:38,552 --> 00:11:39,573
What?

209
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:42,805
Do you want me to do that?

210
00:11:45,191 --> 00:11:46,214
I don't know.

211
00:11:47,049 --> 00:11:48,319
All I want...

212
00:11:49,038 --> 00:11:51,431
is for Ji Ni's marrow to match O Reum's,

213
00:11:52,625 --> 00:11:54,695
no matter the circumstances
of Ji Ni's birth.

214
00:11:55,315 --> 00:11:56,358
That's all.

215
00:11:56,772 --> 00:11:58,999
- Seung Hyun.
- I know how you feel, Mom.

216
00:12:01,458 --> 00:12:03,156
I'll get ready and go to the hospital.

217
00:12:19,365 --> 00:12:21,178
We're at the beach now.

218
00:12:21,392 --> 00:12:23,530
It's day two at the beach.

219
00:12:23,892 --> 00:12:27,518
Right. We're on day two
of our planning meeting.

220
00:12:29,545 --> 00:12:30,668
What are you talking about?

221
00:12:31,069 --> 00:12:33,269
Where's Ji Ni?
Why are you talking nonsense?

222
00:12:34,138 --> 00:12:37,058
I told you, we're all with Ji Ni
on a three-day planning trip.

223
00:12:37,745 --> 00:12:39,505
Can't you hear the waves?

224
00:12:42,479 --> 00:12:44,818
It's so fun teasing you.

225
00:12:48,951 --> 00:12:52,398
Really? Then is Ji Ni going
to have her bone marrow taken now?

226
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:55,927
Keep your voice down. Walls have ears.

227
00:12:57,378 --> 00:13:00,816
Mother Teresa, Princess Diana,
and Na Ji Ni...

228
00:13:00,903 --> 00:13:02,257
are basically in the same league.

229
00:13:02,345 --> 00:13:03,698
What kind of child is he?

230
00:13:03,752 --> 00:13:05,993
That's top secret too.

231
00:13:06,638 --> 00:13:09,976
You met Ji Ni's mother before
and heard why Do Hee did that, right?

232
00:13:10,475 --> 00:13:13,487
- Yes.
- So you know a bit about Ji Ni's family.

233
00:13:14,165 --> 00:13:16,549
He's from that family,

234
00:13:16,552 --> 00:13:18,793
the son of someone who's like
an older brother to Ji Ni.

235
00:13:18,802 --> 00:13:20,879
They got close at the funeral.

236
00:13:21,238 --> 00:13:22,727
Fate must have known,

237
00:13:22,802 --> 00:13:25,300
and brought them together.

238
00:13:26,287 --> 00:13:27,503
Any side effects?

239
00:13:28,465 --> 00:13:31,291
I asked too.
Thankfully, they said she'll be fine.

240
00:13:31,652 --> 00:13:32,701
And hey,

241
00:13:33,042 --> 00:13:36,332
do you think someone willing
to donate marrow would care?

242
00:13:37,205 --> 00:13:38,605
So which hospital is she at?

243
00:13:41,938 --> 00:13:43,556
It's Ji Ni's mother.

244
00:13:43,559 --> 00:13:45,405
Come on, answer it.

245
00:13:46,792 --> 00:13:49,898
I can't lie with so many people watching.

246
00:13:55,018 --> 00:13:56,313
Yes, ma'am.

247
00:13:57,248 --> 00:13:59,518
You can't reach Ji Ni, right?

248
00:14:00,152 --> 00:14:03,305
I didn't want to stay in the meeting,
so I slipped out early.

249
00:14:04,925 --> 00:14:07,065
Ji Ni won't be able to answer right now.

250
00:14:07,305 --> 00:14:09,355
She's working really hard in the meeting.

251
00:14:10,627 --> 00:14:11,811
Yes, ma'am.

252
00:14:12,405 --> 00:14:14,318
Yes, have a good evening.

253
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:15,971
Goodbye.

254
00:14:19,078 --> 00:14:20,558
Hey, what did she say?

255
00:14:21,299 --> 00:14:22,558
She said she understands.

256
00:14:30,852 --> 00:14:31,886
Honey,

257
00:14:32,367 --> 00:14:35,005
it feels strange
with no one home for days.

258
00:14:59,105 --> 00:15:00,241
If you develop a high fever,

259
00:15:00,243 --> 00:15:02,730
or notice bleeding from the treated area,
come to the hospital right away.

260
00:15:02,733 --> 00:15:03,733
Okay.

261
00:15:04,401 --> 00:15:06,491
- Thank you.
- Thank you. Take care.

262
00:15:42,858 --> 00:15:45,314
It looks like she was already discharged.

263
00:15:45,316 --> 00:15:46,608
Thank you.

264
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:52,606
Has Na Ji Ni left?

265
00:15:52,608 --> 00:15:55,733
One moment. Yes, she was just discharged.

266
00:15:56,025 --> 00:15:57,483
Thank you.

267
00:16:23,126 --> 00:16:24,339
Ji Ni!

268
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,280
This isn't our department's ward,

269
00:16:40,608 --> 00:16:42,908
but there were no rooms available,
so we had to use this one.

270
00:16:43,441 --> 00:16:44,816
She's going to be okay, right?

271
00:16:45,417 --> 00:16:47,355
If she needs more tests or anything,
please do them.

272
00:16:47,365 --> 00:16:48,558
Are you her boyfriend?

273
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,740
Yes. What?

274
00:16:51,066 --> 00:16:52,312
No...

275
00:16:52,691 --> 00:16:54,400
We're just acquaintances.

276
00:16:54,441 --> 00:16:56,439
Then I guess you don't know
why she was hospitalized.

277
00:16:56,441 --> 00:16:58,808
I know.

278
00:17:00,566 --> 00:17:02,275
She may develop anemia
and low blood pressure,

279
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:05,022
so she needs to take it easy
for a few days and eat well.

280
00:17:05,340 --> 00:17:06,672
Don't worry.

281
00:17:08,116 --> 00:17:10,679
If you're going to date her,
you'd better stay on my good side.

282
00:17:11,070 --> 00:17:13,587
I'm the closest thing she has to a father.

283
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:18,441
Yes, I understand.

284
00:17:18,608 --> 00:17:20,556
Why are you being so vague?

285
00:17:20,650 --> 00:17:22,422
Be clear.

286
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,683
Yes, I will.

287
00:17:25,941 --> 00:17:27,316
Don't worry too much.

288
00:17:27,733 --> 00:17:29,898
Once this IV is finished, she can go home.

289
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:31,398
I told her to rest a little longer,

290
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:34,108
but she insisted on going home
because of her mom, so I discharged her.

291
00:17:34,691 --> 00:17:36,525
Can you stay until the IV is finished?

292
00:17:36,533 --> 00:17:38,387
Of course. I'll stay with her.

293
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:40,131
Go back to work, Doctor.

294
00:17:40,691 --> 00:17:42,495
Call me if anything happens.

295
00:17:42,983 --> 00:17:43,983
Okay.

296
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:57,766
Na Ji Ni,

297
00:17:58,775 --> 00:18:01,316
are you noble or just reckless?

298
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:36,644
Dad.

299
00:19:37,741 --> 00:19:38,937
O Reum.

300
00:19:40,525 --> 00:19:41,800
Don't go.

301
00:19:44,108 --> 00:19:46,464
O Reum.

302
00:20:00,483 --> 00:20:01,483
(Do Hee)

303
00:20:09,181 --> 00:20:11,281
I'm sorry. You should be sleeping.
Did I wake you?

304
00:20:11,283 --> 00:20:12,283
Are you okay?

305
00:20:14,233 --> 00:20:15,441
Nothing happened.

306
00:20:15,733 --> 00:20:16,998
Dr. Hwang...

307
00:20:17,191 --> 00:20:19,356
told me to contact him, so I did.

308
00:20:19,358 --> 00:20:21,481
He stopped by.
He said you just need to rest.

309
00:20:21,483 --> 00:20:23,985
He said you might develop anemia
and low blood pressure.

310
00:20:25,892 --> 00:20:26,944
That's all.

311
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:30,500
Okay.

312
00:20:31,142 --> 00:20:33,075
Just stay until it's finished.

313
00:20:33,283 --> 00:20:34,777
Dr. Hwang told me to do that.

314
00:20:37,691 --> 00:20:39,314
How did you get here?

315
00:20:39,316 --> 00:20:41,804
I just heard what happened and came over.

316
00:20:42,691 --> 00:20:44,992
I came to support you,

317
00:20:45,316 --> 00:20:46,817
then I found you nearby.

318
00:20:49,798 --> 00:20:51,632
You didn't have to do that.

319
00:20:55,857 --> 00:20:57,297
Why are you so amazing?

320
00:20:57,358 --> 00:20:58,775
This is a huge deal.

321
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:02,531
That...

322
00:21:03,299 --> 00:21:05,131
Did you do that because of me?

323
00:21:06,525 --> 00:21:08,650
It's a mess, right?

324
00:21:09,691 --> 00:21:12,812
I was worried the sunlight
might disturb your sleep.

325
00:21:17,066 --> 00:21:18,544
I contacted Jung A.

326
00:21:18,908 --> 00:21:20,060
She'll be coming.

327
00:21:20,441 --> 00:21:22,435
You didn't have to do that.

328
00:21:23,415 --> 00:21:24,523
Just lie down a bit longer.

329
00:21:24,775 --> 00:21:26,941
I'm fine. It's nothing serious.

330
00:21:27,775 --> 00:21:29,316
Ji Ni, are you okay?

331
00:21:31,316 --> 00:21:32,635
My dear Ji Ni...

332
00:21:32,858 --> 00:21:34,958
I'm fine. I just felt a little dizzy.

333
00:21:35,483 --> 00:21:38,066
You're incredible.
You're seriously impressive.

334
00:21:38,233 --> 00:21:39,858
I've always wondered
what it was like to faint.

335
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:41,106
How did you collapse?

336
00:21:41,108 --> 00:21:42,983
Did you gasp, or just drop with a thud?

337
00:21:43,858 --> 00:21:46,525
Don't be ridiculous. I'm exhausted.

338
00:21:47,691 --> 00:21:50,035
Why would you come here
without saying anything?

339
00:21:50,358 --> 00:21:52,035
If Do Hee finds out, she'll lose it.

340
00:21:53,063 --> 00:21:54,615
Please don't get us in trouble.

341
00:21:54,691 --> 00:21:56,773
Women are sensitive
about things like this.

342
00:21:56,858 --> 00:21:57,927
Don't worry.

343
00:22:02,608 --> 00:22:04,900
My mom says
you must be having a really hard time.

344
00:22:05,366 --> 00:22:07,552
She told me to make sure you eat well.
Dinner's on me.

345
00:22:08,733 --> 00:22:10,064
Your mom knows too?

346
00:22:10,066 --> 00:22:12,908
Don't worry. I made sure she'd keep quiet.

347
00:22:12,911 --> 00:22:16,504
Anyway, she told me to feed you well.
She even gave me her card.

348
00:22:16,966 --> 00:22:18,712
She says you're a really good person.

349
00:22:18,775 --> 00:22:20,556
Who would do this
for her father's ex-wife's grandson...

350
00:22:22,891 --> 00:22:23,937
You don't want to hear that?

351
00:22:25,150 --> 00:22:26,546
No, not really.

352
00:22:27,733 --> 00:22:29,535
I'm fine, so you two can go.

353
00:22:29,641 --> 00:22:30,746
I'll leave after this IV.

354
00:22:30,750 --> 00:22:32,333
- No way.
- No way.

355
00:22:39,775 --> 00:22:41,481
Ji Ni, you should eat something.

356
00:22:41,483 --> 00:22:42,615
Okay.

357
00:22:43,316 --> 00:22:45,900
Right, we're only eating because of you,

358
00:22:45,908 --> 00:22:47,522
so you need to eat too.

359
00:22:47,525 --> 00:22:49,108
I can finish all of this.

360
00:22:50,650 --> 00:22:51,831
Okay.

361
00:22:52,650 --> 00:22:53,981
Finally ready to indulge.

362
00:22:53,983 --> 00:22:55,941
Beef is good for anemia, so eat up.

363
00:22:56,069 --> 00:22:57,814
But why are you going this far?

364
00:22:57,816 --> 00:22:59,191
I'm really curious.

365
00:23:00,816 --> 00:23:04,189
Humanitarian reasons?
I'm not as selfless as Ji Ni,

366
00:23:04,191 --> 00:23:07,015
but it's kind of like
supporting a soldier at war.

367
00:23:07,691 --> 00:23:10,623
If I help you, it feels like
I've done something good too.

368
00:23:10,733 --> 00:23:12,837
- Like saving a child?
- Bingo.

369
00:23:13,230 --> 00:23:15,022
Of course, you're the one
who actually saved him, Ji Ni.

370
00:23:15,025 --> 00:23:16,956
I think I get that feeling too.

371
00:23:17,575 --> 00:23:20,660
When my friend does something good,
it feels like I did it too.

372
00:23:22,066 --> 00:23:23,191
Here!

373
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:25,108
You eat.

374
00:23:25,191 --> 00:23:27,006
Let me save a little face here.

375
00:23:31,816 --> 00:23:32,877
Today,

376
00:23:33,612 --> 00:23:36,025
it was just a coincidence,
but thank you. Really.

377
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:38,950
But I'd appreciate it...

378
00:23:39,016 --> 00:23:41,317
if you stopped calling me "amazing"
or "incredible."

379
00:23:42,191 --> 00:23:43,906
O Reum doesn't know,

380
00:23:44,025 --> 00:23:46,390
but I know that he and I are family.

381
00:23:46,525 --> 00:23:47,648
Ji Ni.

382
00:23:47,650 --> 00:23:52,275
I've spent my whole life being family
with someone who couldn't acknowledge me.

383
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:54,085
As for my mom and me...

384
00:23:54,616 --> 00:23:58,248
when I was young, I thought she hid me
out of selfishness,

385
00:23:59,066 --> 00:24:02,225
but she was just trying to survive.

386
00:24:04,150 --> 00:24:07,565
The family system has always been
a sore spot for me.

387
00:24:08,441 --> 00:24:11,650
But now, I want to live on my own terms.

388
00:24:12,316 --> 00:24:14,608
So no more compliments, please.

389
00:24:18,316 --> 00:24:20,421
By the time O Reum is old enough
to join the army,

390
00:24:20,483 --> 00:24:22,404
I wonder how proud
you'll feel about today.

391
00:24:23,983 --> 00:24:25,644
That would be wonderful.

392
00:24:28,983 --> 00:24:31,525
Your sudden mood changes
are really something else.

393
00:24:32,208 --> 00:24:33,310
Right.

394
00:24:34,191 --> 00:24:36,406
If O Reum grows up strong
and joins the army,

395
00:24:37,316 --> 00:24:39,202
I think I'll be touched too.

396
00:24:41,483 --> 00:24:42,900
Please eat.

397
00:24:50,858 --> 00:24:52,573
I'm back.

398
00:24:56,066 --> 00:24:57,856
I waited for you
to come back from your meeting.

399
00:24:57,858 --> 00:25:00,271
If my life were any shorter,
I'd have died waiting.

400
00:25:00,932 --> 00:25:02,591
Mom, come on.

401
00:25:05,015 --> 00:25:07,265
You smell like barbecue.

402
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:10,104
You said you had a meeting. You lied.

403
00:25:11,408 --> 00:25:14,191
The CEO treated us to barbecue
for our last dinner.

404
00:25:15,167 --> 00:25:17,523
Are you really doing this?
Why are you sniffing me?

405
00:25:17,525 --> 00:25:19,025
Was it really a meeting?

406
00:25:19,316 --> 00:25:21,262
You're not dating behind my back, are you?

407
00:25:21,265 --> 00:25:23,816
That's what you would've done
behind grandma's back.

408
00:25:24,191 --> 00:25:26,191
Not me. I hate love.

409
00:25:26,608 --> 00:25:29,915
I'll never break your heart
over a relationship, so don't worry.

410
00:25:30,566 --> 00:25:32,691
You still have to love someone.

411
00:25:33,191 --> 00:25:35,522
Mom, I'm tired.

412
00:25:35,525 --> 00:25:37,633
I'm going to wash up and sleep,
so don't follow me.

413
00:25:37,675 --> 00:25:39,858
I waited for you all day, you brat.

414
00:25:40,066 --> 00:25:41,650
Mom, practice.

415
00:25:41,858 --> 00:25:43,849
Play the cello you love.

416
00:25:44,968 --> 00:25:46,350
That brat...

417
00:25:48,909 --> 00:25:50,030
Seriously.

418
00:25:53,775 --> 00:25:56,736
Honey, can you believe this?

419
00:25:57,261 --> 00:25:58,816
Say something to her.

420
00:26:00,775 --> 00:26:02,809
I wasn't going to drink today.

421
00:26:05,025 --> 00:26:07,566
But now I have no choice.

422
00:26:08,191 --> 00:26:09,941
Wine again?

423
00:26:10,191 --> 00:26:12,441
Stop drinking so much.

424
00:26:12,900 --> 00:26:14,691
You'll get gout at this rate.

425
00:26:14,949 --> 00:26:17,033
You little brat.
Why do you always come after me?

426
00:26:18,316 --> 00:26:20,483
Tell me about the planning meeting.

427
00:26:20,900 --> 00:26:23,688
I've been alone all day.
I'm dying to talk.

428
00:26:23,691 --> 00:26:25,889
I told you, we're making a folktale.

429
00:26:26,900 --> 00:26:29,298
Our CEO likes history books,

430
00:26:29,400 --> 00:26:32,233
so we talked about editing some folktales.

431
00:26:34,358 --> 00:26:36,146
Read a book and go to bed, Mom.

432
00:26:36,775 --> 00:26:37,921
I'm going to sleep.

433
00:26:40,275 --> 00:26:41,585
That brat.

434
00:26:48,775 --> 00:26:51,441
Na Se Ri, you need to get used to this.

435
00:26:52,233 --> 00:26:55,233
You need to get used to this.

436
00:27:17,983 --> 00:27:20,775
Dad, I did the right thing, right?

437
00:27:21,674 --> 00:27:25,174
I didn't think about them
or our situation.

438
00:27:27,066 --> 00:27:28,517
My bone marrow...

439
00:27:29,441 --> 00:27:31,760
Please help the transplant
go well for O Reum.

440
00:27:32,650 --> 00:27:34,858
Help me until the end, Dad.

441
00:27:57,816 --> 00:28:01,066
(Family Register)

442
00:28:01,150 --> 00:28:02,339
I said no.

443
00:28:02,525 --> 00:28:03,564
And you're still telling me to go?

444
00:28:03,566 --> 00:28:05,064
Pressuring mom like this...

445
00:28:05,066 --> 00:28:06,398
feels cruel to me.

446
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:09,862
You said you'd think about it
if I apologized for insulting Ji Ni.

447
00:28:09,864 --> 00:28:11,105
Please hold on a little longer.

448
00:28:11,108 --> 00:28:12,356
Then what about your mom?

449
00:28:12,358 --> 00:28:13,814
Are the results not out yet?

450
00:28:13,816 --> 00:28:15,606
It must be hard for everyone waiting.

451
00:28:15,608 --> 00:28:17,564
You think you can just have another child.

452
00:28:17,566 --> 00:28:19,731
Mother, I'm sorry.

453
00:28:19,733 --> 00:28:22,444
I gave birth to a sick child. I'm sorry.

454
00:28:22,525 --> 00:28:23,941
I was happy.

455
00:28:25,146 --> 00:28:27,516
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
